[GloomhavenVR][Env] Cellar rat — a SCHEDULE, not a loop (user: "mehr random statt immer den selben weg"). Everything below is H(slot,k) of the SHARED clock alone (_Time.y+_GhvrTimeOfs, slot = floor(t/26 s)): no Random, no per-client state, no sin() in the hash, so two clients compute the same bits.
  ROUTES: a continuum, not a list — P1 wanders +-0.50/0.80 m about (-0.46,0.00), P2 +-0.12/0.32 m about (-0.12,0.28); up to 1.01 m of lateral spread, arc length 5.74..14.21 m (the single old route was 9.90 m). 2541 of the 2541 crossings below take a route no other one takes, measured to the nearest cm.
  MODES over 3000 slots: 2541 crossings (15% of slots quiet), 43% out of the south hole instead of the north, 30% turn back into the hole they came from at u=0.35..0.75, 32% of all crossings (= 45% of the straight ones) stop to sniff.
  TIMING: gap between crossings 12..111 s (median 27 s); each lasts 2.4..9.2 s at 1.33..3.01 m/s; latest a run can still be going is 23.2 s of the 26 s slot.
  CLEARANCE, over the WHOLE family and not just one route: play-space 3.30 m (needs >= 3.25); side walls 1.25 m (the 0.06 m in z is the two HOLES, which are in the wall on purpose); props Barrel0 0.35 m (its (-3.41,-3.00) against u=0.77), Barrel1 0.29 m (its (-3.91,-1.89) against u=0.65), Barrel2 0.13 m (its (-2.66,-3.51) against u=0.85), Bucket 1.30 m (its (-3.88,-3.93) against u=0.80) (the crates are exempt — it ends under them on purpose). Moon-beam axis 0.11..0.48 m, 100% of crossings inside the 0.80 m the beam lights.
  HAUNT — THE STARE: 149 of the 2541 crossings (6%, about one in 17) stop mid-floor and turn the head toward the ROOM CENTRE for ~1 s — never toward the camera, which would be the billboard behaviour this project has ruled out and would point somewhere else on every client. Gated on the haunt master AND on a QUIET haunt slot, so it can never land on top of one of the six drawn events; at the shipped dial (0.50) that costs it about half its rolls. Every 26 s slot, so roughly one stare every 9 min.
